Spring REST
Spring REST is a module in Spring Framework basically used to create restful web services that expose resources over HTTP using HTTP standard methods and exchange data mainly in JSON format.

What is REST (Representational State transfer)
Rest is a architectural style for designing destributed system where the resource are exposed by the URLs and manipulated by using standard HTTP mnethods.

Why Only spring REST?
Spring REST simplifies the development of restful web services by providing annotations, automatic conversion to JSON, better exception handling and tight integration with Spring BOOT and Spring Data JPA.

Advantages of using Spring REST
1. Automatic Conversion to JSON(serialization and desrialization)
2. Easy and better exception handling 
3. Reduces Boilerplate Code
4. Easy request Mapping 

In short,
REST api Basically allows multiple/ heterogeneous technologies to interact/connect with each other.
rest can send any type of data xml, text, image etc

Annontations
@RestController -- specialized annontation that combines both @Controller and @ResponseBody allows method to directly map the data instead of views.
@GetMapping -- to get the resource
@PostMapping --creates the new resource
@PutMapping -- update the existing respurce completely
@PatchMapping -- update the existing resource partially
@DeleteMapping -- delete the existing resoource
@RequestMapping -- to map the url
@PathVariable -- take the data from the url 
@RequestParam -- reads query parameter from the URLs


GET is idemPotent and post is not
Idemponent : is an operation that can be applied multiple times without changing the output

Rest follows Stateless Protocol
Rest has stateless protocol means the server does not store any client data during request

What is ResponseEntity
A class the returns complete HTTP resource including HTTPStatus code , headers and body

